 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2021-03-08",
   "text": "Ending Debt Collection Harassment Act of 2021\n This bill prohibits a debt collector from sending electronic communications to a consumer without the consumer's consent. The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) may not issue rules that allow a debt collector to send unlimited electronic communications. Additionally, the CFPB must report on consumer complaints about electronic communications and enforcement actions taken against debt collectors."
  }
 ],
